<h1>Comparative Quotation — Warehouse PDA Devices</h1>

<div class="meta">
  <p><strong>Prepared for:</strong> Double-Y IT Systems / Parisi Warehouse Project<br>
  <strong>Delivery location:</strong> Sydney, NSW, Australia<br>
  <strong>Date:</strong> 9 July 2026<br>
  <strong>Reference:</strong> RFQ-PDA-SYD-2026-07-09<br>
  <strong>Quantity required:</strong> 10 handheld PDA units (identical configuration per supplier)</p>
</div>

<h2>1. Purpose</h2>
<p>This document compares indicative quotations from three Sydney-area suppliers for <strong>10 rugged Android warehouse PDAs</strong> suitable for barcode scanning, Wi-Fi connectivity, and integration with a warehouse management system (WMS). The devices are intended for in-warehouse use (four walls), including receiving, put-away, picking, and stocktake operations.</p>

<h2>2. Standard Technical Requirement (all suppliers)</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Android-based rugged handheld computer (business class, not consumer smartphone)</li>
  <li>Integrated 2D barcode imager (1D/2D, QR, Code128, EAN, etc.)</li>
  <li>Wi-Fi 802.11 a/b/g/n/ac (dual band preferred)</li>
  <li>Minimum 4 GB RAM / 64 GB storage (or equivalent)</li>
  <li>5-inch colour touchscreen, glove-friendly</li>
  <li>IP65 or better ingress protection; 1.2 m+ drop spec</li>
  <li>Rechargeable battery for a full warehouse shift (8+ hours)</li>
  <li>USB/data/charging capability and manufacturer warranty (minimum 12 months)</li>
  <li>Pre-staging: Wi-Fi profile, barcode test, optional WMS client install</li>
</ul>

