<h2>7. HARMONiQ Mobile Warehouse — Compatibility Assessment</h2>

<p>This section evaluates whether the three quoted PDA models are suitable for <strong>HARMONiQ Mobile Warehouse</strong> (WT170), as documented for the Parisi warehouse environment. Reference: <em>HARMONiQ Mobile Warehouse</em> user guide (Parisi project documentation).</p>

<h3>7.1 How HARMONiQ uses PDAs (architecture)</h3>
<p>HARMONiQ Mobile Warehouse does <strong>not</strong> run as a native Android application on the device. According to the official setup guide, the typical deployment is:</p>
<ol>
  <li>Each PDA connects via <strong>Microsoft Remote Desktop (RDP)</strong> to a <strong>Windows terminal server</strong> where HARMONiQ is installed.</li>
  <li>Each warehouse operator requires a <strong>Windows Active Directory</strong> user account authorised for the terminal server.</li>
  <li>HARMONiQ is configured on the server: <strong>PDA menus</strong>, <strong>roles</strong> (Custom Mobile Menu), and <strong>user assignments</strong> (functions prefixed with <strong>MWH</strong>).</li>
  <li>Operators work inside the RDP session: Stock Inquiries, Picking Notes, Goods In, Stock Take, Packing, etc.</li>
  <li>The barcode imager must send scanned data into the <strong>active RDP window</strong> (keyboard wedge / data capture profile).</li>
</ol>
<p>RDP connection settings documented: <strong>High Color</strong>, <strong>Full Screen</strong>, <strong>Fit remote desktop to screen</strong>.</p>

