<h3>7.3 Scanner configuration (critical for HARMONiQ)</h3>
<p>HARMONiQ workflows rely on the <strong>Scan</strong> button and barcode fields inside the RDP session (picking, goods in, stocktake, packing). The imager must deliver scan data to the foreground RDP application:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Zebra TC21:</strong> configure <strong>DataWedge</strong> profile targeting the Remote Desktop client package; enable keyboard output with suffix (e.g. Enter).</li>
  <li><strong>Honeywell CT45 XP:</strong> configure <strong>Velocity</strong> or enterprise keyboard wedge profile for the RDP client.</li>
  <li><strong>CipherLab RK25:</strong> configure reader service / wedge mode for the installed RDP application.</li>
</ul>
<p>Request each supplier to include <strong>HARMONiQ RDP scan profile setup</strong> in their staging quote (or as a billable professional service line item).</p>

<h3>7.4 Infrastructure prerequisites (not included in hardware quotes)</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Windows terminal server hosting HARMONiQ (RDS / Remote Desktop Services)</li>
  <li>Active Directory user accounts — one per PDA operator</li>
  <li>Stable warehouse Wi-Fi with coverage at all bin locations</li>
  <li>HARMONiQ PDA menus, roles, and MWH functions configured by ERP administrator</li>
  <li>Product barcodes in HARMONiQ aligned with physical labels (Parisi catalogue / BARCODEPARISI)</li>
  <li>RDP/CAL licensing as required by Microsoft licensing model in use</li>
</ul>

