<h3>7.7 Recommended pre-purchase validation (POC checklist)</h3>
<p>Before purchasing all 10 units, complete a <strong>1-device proof of concept</strong> on the live (or UAT) HARMONiQ terminal server:</p>
<ol>
  <li>Install Microsoft Remote Desktop (or approved RDP client) on the trial PDA.</li>
  <li>Connect to the HARMONiQ terminal server (High Color, Full Screen, Fit to screen).</li>
  <li>Log in with an AD test user assigned a Mobile Warehouse role.</li>
  <li>Open <strong>Stock Inquiries</strong> → scan a known Parisi product barcode → confirm product resolves correctly.</li>
  <li>Open <strong>Picking Note</strong> (test environment) → scan item → confirm quantity entry works.</li>
  <li>Test Wi-Fi roaming between two warehouse zones during an active RDP session.</li>
  <li>Confirm session reconnect behaviour after brief Wi-Fi drop (warehouse reality).</li>
  <li>Obtain written confirmation from the <strong>HARMONiQ implementer / VAR</strong> that the selected model is accepted for production use.</li>
</ol>

<p><strong>Conclusion:</strong> All three quoted PDA models are <strong>technically suitable</strong> for HARMONiQ Mobile Warehouse under the documented <strong>RDP + 2D scanner + Wi-Fi</strong> architecture. They are <strong>not plug-and-play certified</strong> in the WT170 manual (no specific device list). Pilot testing and implementer sign-off are mandatory before full deployment.</p>

